  "scope": "The exact frozen source checked_q(k) calls Q::from_limbs(limbs_of(k)).ok_or(()), and limbs_of returns k.c0.a, k.c0.b, k.c1.a, k.c1.b in that order. The Lean theorem instantiates candidate Q.from_limbs on the exact same ordered current QM31 U32 projections. For any current q with four coordinates below m31Modulus it proves the child returns the exact source-limb array; strict parser success on the same q supplies those four bounds via installed_parser_success_strict. Thus a successful parser result yields successful candidate validation with the same four coordinate values. The outer Rust ok_or wrapper and full checked_q parent dispatch are handled by the stronger existing CandidatePushCheckedQBridge packet; no claim of full S4/caller closure."
